{
  "tema": 6332,
  "slug": "que-causa",
  "titulo": "Que to express cause",
  "subtitulo": "Apúrate, que se va el camión.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Que (no accent) can introduce a reason, like porque, especially after a command or a statement: Me voy, que tengo que trabajar. It's informal and goes after the main clause.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In conversation, **que** can work like **porque** to explain **why**:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "[statement / command]",
            ", que",
            "+ reason"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It goes **after** the main clause, usually after a comma, and it's informal. It's very common after commands: **Apúrate, que...**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**No accent**: it's a conjunction, not a question word."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **que** here is a shrug that adds _because..._"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Me voy al súper, ==que== tengo que hacer el mandado.",
              "en": "I'm going to the supermarket, I have to do the shopping."
            },
            {
              "es": "Pónganse a estudiar, ==que== tienen mucho que aprender.",
              "en": "Get studying, you have a lot to learn."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy no vine a trabajar, ==que== estoy enfermo.",
              "en": "I didn't come to work today, I'm sick."
            },
            {
              "es": "Voy a hablar con la maestra, ==que== no entiendo nada.",
              "en": "I'm going to talk to the teacher, because I don't understand a thing."
            },
            {
              "es": "Apúrate, ==que== se va el camión.",
              "en": "Hurry up, the bus is leaving."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ponte el suéter, ==que== hace frío.",
              "en": "Put on your sweater, it's cold."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "porque",
      "titulo": "Same as porque",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "que",
                  "t": "Voy a hablar con la maestra, que no entiendo nada."
                },
                {
                  "v": "porque",
                  "t": "Voy a hablar con la maestra, porque no entiendo nada."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Same meaning; **que** is more casual."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Abrígate, qué hace frío."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Abrígate, que hace frío."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "No accent."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
